    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class in the project (the other files under `acceptance/` are an abstract base and a helper), and both of its tests pass, including the two new `locality` checkpoints.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `locality` field is a read-only, derived owner attribute returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`. I implemented it following the existing pattern used for the other derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the MapStruct-consumed `OwnerDto` is generated with a `locality` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus the fixed city-to-region table and a `locality(owner)` default method:\n   - `Sydney \u2192 NSW`, `Melbourne \u2192 VIC`, `Brisbane \u2192 QLD`\n   - any other (or absent) city \u2192 `\"UNKNOWN\"`\n\nThis matches the test's pinned `CITY_REGION` table exactly (case-sensitive `Map.get`-style lookup), so `Sydney` derives `NSW` and the random `Town<seq>` cities derive `UNKNOWN`.",
